  "body": "## What happens\n\n#4341 adds a Z retract before the preamble `G49` of each later section in the Mazak, Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts. Other posts also write `G49` in each section preamble, then `T M6`, with no Z retract before it:\n\n- `assets/posts/haas.cps` (`G17 G90 G94 <wcs> G40 G49 G80`)\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`G17 G90 <wcs> G40 G49 G80`)\n- `assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps` (`G49` when the tool length offset is used)\n\n`assets/posts/mach4.cps` writes `G49` only in the program header, before the first tool. It is not in this list.\n\n## Expected\n\nFor each post, find out from the public manual of the control if a `G49` block with no axis word moves Z.\n\n- If it moves Z, retract Z before the `G49`, as #4341 does. A test pins it.\n- If it does not move Z, record the post as not affected, with the manual section.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The #4341 decision record: `docs/decisions/4341-mazak-retract-before-toolchange.md`.\n- The #4341 scope was the Mazak audit (#4130). These posts were not checked.\n",
